1
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:13,780
More and more people think that life is better in the city than the countryside.

2
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:21,687
For the first time in history more than 50% of the world’s population lives in urban areas.

3
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:28,480
However, there are still many groups of people who live in some of the wildest places on the planet.

4
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:34,980
The Kalahari is a large area of bush land in southern Africa.

5
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:37,036
It has two parts.

6
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:43,027
The south part is drier than the north and plants do not grow there very well.

7
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:50,736
Every year at the end of summer it rains and the land becomes more beautiful than at other times of the year.

8
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:55,820
But the grass and the bushes soon get dry and turn brown again.

9
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:58,100
Life there is difficult.

10
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,984
The San are a group of people who live in the Kalahari.

11
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:09,240
They live in huts, eat wild animals – even lions – plants and berries.

12
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,820
They are very good with bows and arrows, and use them for hunting.

13
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:20,060
Up in the mountains of central Papua New Guinea is the Chimbu Province.

14
00:01:21,080 --> 00:01:24,840
This jungle area is one of the world’s most remote places.

15
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:30,186
It is also home to Mt Wilhelm, the highest mountain on the island.

16
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:34,660
Several different tribes live in the valleys between the mountains.

17
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:38,780
One of these is the Chimbu skeleton dancers.

18
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:41,760
They paint skeletons onto their bodies.

19
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:47,578
This makes them look scarier and it frightens other people away from their land.

20
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:55,100
The Yamal Peninsula in northern Siberia is one and a half times bigger than France.

21
00:01:56,120 --> 00:02:02,300
It is frozen for much of the year and temperatures can reach -50°C in the winter.

22
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:08,720
But this area is home to a tribe of about 10,000 people called the Nenets.

23
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:15,047
The Nenets are nomadic, meaning they frequently move from one place to another.

24
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:23,615
Each year around 300,000 reindeer move around the land and the Nenets always go with them.

25
00:02:24,740 --> 00:02:31,069
The recent discovery of gas in the area means more people than before are visiting the Yamal.

26
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:35,249
So the Nenets now have more contact with the outside world.

27
00:02:36,860 --> 00:02:41,040
The Bayan-Ölgii Province is the highest part of Mongolia.

28
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:46,580
It is a wild area with many mountains, lakes, forests and rivers.

29
00:02:47,420 --> 00:02:51,119
It is also home to the Kazakh golden eagle hunters.

30
00:02:52,020 --> 00:02:58,640
These people travel around the mountains and use eagles to hunt for foxes and other small animals.

31
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:03,844
When boys turn 13, they can become golden eagle hunters.

32
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:11,599
However, they have to be stronger than most boys their age because they have to show that they can carry the weight of an eagle.

33
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:20,160
There are about 100,000 Kazakh people, but only around 250 of them are golden eagle hunters.
